; Find the objects the noun phrases of a sentence mean
;
; The noun matcher of a command. #R$7CCB returns the next candidate that fits
; the first noun phrase and that the verb lets through (NZ, the object in
; FirstObject; Z when the candidates are used up). When the command takes a
; second noun (#R$7AD8) a candidate is kept only if #R$7D17 finds a second-noun
; candidate that the whole command allows with it (#R$7ABA starts that scan);
; otherwise the candidate is kept when the check #R$7AED passes with it alone.
; Kept first candidates are counted in RecWork3 ($7940), the last one in
; RecWork7 ($7956). When the candidates are used up, exactly one must have
; been kept: it becomes FirstObject. The second noun is then settled the same
; way: kept candidates counted in $7941, the last one in RecWork8 ($7957), and
; exactly one goes to SecondObject.
; .
; With ALL typed (RecWork5 is 1) the first kept candidate is returned at once.
; The scan position (RecPtr1) is not cleared by #R$79A9, so the next call goes
; on with the next object. No candidate, or more than one, gives NZ, and the
; caller (#R$79B6) hands over to #R$7DBC, which tells the player ("I see
; nothing to ...", or asks what is meant).
; .
; Hardware: none.
;
; RecBuf1 Words of the first noun phrase (RecBuf2 for the second)
; O:F Z when the objects are found (FirstObject, SecondObject), NZ when they are not
@label=ResolveNouns
c$7A14 CALL $7CCB    ; next candidate for the first noun: NZ found
 $7A17 JR NZ,$7A2E   ;
 $7A19 LD A,($7940)  ; none left: how many were accepted?
 $7A1C CP $01        ;
 $7A1E RET NZ        ; not exactly one: failure
 $7A1F LD A,($7956)  ; the one accepted object
 $7A22 LD ($B6E8),A  ; FirstObject
 $7A25 CALL $7ABA    ; StartNounScan2
 $7A28 CALL $7AD8    ; NeedSecondNoun
 $7A2B JR NZ,$7A55   ; yes: pick the second
 $7A2D RET           ; no: done (Z)
*$7A2E LD HL,$793F   ; RecWork2: candidates seen for the first noun
 $7A31 INC (HL)      ;
 $7A32 CALL $7AD8    ; NeedSecondNoun
 $7A35 JR Z,$7A50    ; no: test the command with this candidate
 $7A37 CALL $7ABA    ; StartNounScan2
 $7A3A CALL $7D17    ; a candidate for the second noun?
@label=ResolveNouns_Accept
*$7A3D JR Z,$7A14    ; none (or the command was refused): the next first candidate
 $7A3F LD A,($7953)  ; RecWork5: ALL?
 $7A42 DEC A         ;
 $7A43 RET Z         ; ALL: this one, now (Z)
 $7A44 LD A,($B6E8)  ; count this candidate
 $7A47 LD ($7956),A  ;
 $7A4A LD HL,$7940   ;
 $7A4D INC (HL)      ;
 $7A4E JR $7A14      ;
*$7A50 CALL $7AED    ; RunCheck: Z when refused
 $7A53 JR $7A3D      ;
@label=ResolveNouns_Second
*$7A55 CALL $7D17    ; next candidate for the second noun: NZ found
 $7A58 JR NZ,$7A67   ;
 $7A5A LD A,($7941)  ; none left: how many?
 $7A5D CP $01        ;
 $7A5F RET NZ        ; not exactly one: failure
 $7A60 LD A,($7957)  ;
 $7A63 LD ($B6E9),A  ; SecondObject
 $7A66 RET           ; Z: done
*$7A67 LD A,($B6E9)  ; count this candidate
 $7A6A LD ($7957),A  ;
 $7A6D LD HL,$7941   ;
 $7A70 INC (HL)      ;
 $7A71 JR $7A55      ;
